Q: Laravel teardown API calls on reversing migration A: <p>This is going to be an opinionated answer, but I usually do not do any refresh or rollback commands after the initial database design has been created.</p>
<p>And as pointed out in the comments, the <code>migrate:fresh</code> command is a structural change, so laravel's event listener cannot pickup your model changes.</p>
<p>What you can do is to create a custom command to delete all models before executing <code>migrate:fresh</code>.</p>
<pre><code>class MigrateFreshWithItems extends Command
{
    protected $signature = 'migrate:fresh-with-items';

    public function handle()
    {
        Item::all()-&gt;each(function(Item $item) { $item-&gt;delete(); });
        \Artisan::call('migrate:fresh');
    }
}
</code></pre>

Q: How does $this-&gt;db-&gt;trans_status() work in codeigniter transactions? A: <p>This is a mess:</p>

<pre><code>if($status)
    $query_string = 'COMMIT;';
else // darn our update must have failed
    $dba-&gt;execute($query_string);
</code></pre>

<p>Maybe you want:</p>

<pre><code>if($status)
    $query_string = 'COMMIT';
else // darn our update must have failed
    $query_string = 'ROLLBACK';

$dba-&gt;execute($query_string);
</code></pre>

Q: How to change the color of a calculation result depending on a threshold, in Javascript A: <p>There are several issues:</p>
<p>Use delegation
Use querySelectorAll to grab the values.<br />
Calculate the average directly - switch is not needed.
Make sure to convert result to number before comparing.
You need to change the colour of the output, not the input</p>
<p>I guessed some HTML to test and added some test functions. If you paste a complete example I can fix that instead of guessing.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const table = document.getElementById('calcTable');
const threshold = 154;

// helper to get all input values for a column
const getColumnValues = col =&gt; Array.from(
  table.querySelectorAll(`input.val[data-col="${col}"]`),
  el =&gt; Number(el.value) // call back 
).filter(n =&gt; !Number.isNaN(n));

// calculations
const avg = arr =&gt; arr.length ? arr.reduce((a, b) =&gt; a + b, 0) / arr.length : 0;

const std = arr =&gt; {
  const m = avg(arr);
  if (!m &amp;&amp; !arr.some(n =&gt; n !== 0)) return 0; // empty or all zero
  const variance = avg(arr.map(x =&gt; (x - m) ** 2));
  return Math.sqrt(variance);
};

const cv = arr =&gt; {
  const m = avg(arr);
  return m ? std(arr) / m : 0;
};

const min = arr =&gt; (arr.length ? Math.min(...arr) : 0);
const max = arr =&gt; (arr.length ? Math.max(...arr) : 0);

// update all 5 calculation rows for all 7 columns
const recalc = () =&gt; {
  for (let col = 1; col &lt;= 7; col++) {
    const values = getColumnValues(col);
    if (!values.length) continue;

    const results = {
      avg: avg(values),
      std: std(values),
      cv: cv(values),
      min: min(values),
      max: max(values)
    };

    Object.entries(results).forEach(([cls, val]) =&gt; {
      const cell = table.querySelector(`tr.${cls} td[data-col="${col}"]`);
      if (!cell) return;
      const num = Number(val) || 0; // make sure we compare a number
      cell.textContent = num.toFixed(2);
      // colour the *output* cell based on the numeric value
      cell.style.color = num &gt; threshold ? 'red' : 'green';
    });
  }
};

// delegated input event
table.addEventListener('input', e =&gt; {
  if (e.target.matches('.val')) recalc();
});</code></pre>
